_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cure/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cure/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cure/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cure/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cure/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cure/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cure/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think we're missing a .goreleaser.yml file in the repo. I propose one with these contents:\r\n\r\n```\r\nbuilds:\r\n  - main: cmd/headscale/headscale.go\r\n    mod_timestamp: '{{ .CommitTimestamp }}'\r\n    goarch:\r\n      - amd64\r\n      - arm64\r\n    goos:\r\n      - linux\r\n```\r\nOnly the line that sets `main` is strictly necessary. The `mod_timestamp` line is nice so that we make reproducible builds. The `goarch` and `goos` values are there to limit the number of targets we build for.\r\n\r\nI tested this in a dummy repo by playing around with `goreleaser --snapshot --skip-publish --rm-dist` and after setting a local tag, `goreleaser --skip-publish --rm-dist`.","commit_id":"42e147e46fd8a69f58d0dc7f92f16b75a38b1f44","state":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/35#pullrequestreview-682468573","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/35","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/35#pullrequestreview-682468573"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/35"}},"submitted_at":"2021-06-14T01:28:32Z","updated_at":"2021-06-14T01:28:32Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","event":"reviewed"},{"sha":"da8014074cee0b15306df8dc8aa7b076c7caf153","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MjczODcxODU5OmRhODAxNDA3NGNlZTBiMTUzMDZkZjhkYzhhYTdiMDc2YzdjYWYxNTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/da8014074cee0b15